&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to democratize finance for all. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cerulli.com/press-releases/cerulli-anticipates-124-trillion-in-wealth-will-transfer-through-2048&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;An estimated $124 trillion of assets&lt;/a&gt; will be inherited by younger generations in the next two decades. The largest transfer of wealth in human history. If you’re ready to be at the epicenter of this historic cultural and financial shift, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team + role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world&#39;s biggest financial problems. We&#39;re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it&#39;s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We&#39;re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Internal Audit team helps &lt;strong&gt;Robinhood&lt;/strong&gt; meet a complex set of global regulations for crypto-assets and payment services. Our mission is to give the Board of Directors, its Committees and company leadership independent, objective and timely assurance that our governance, risk management and internal controls work as intended, so we can spot new risks early and keep strengthening our control environment!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As &lt;strong&gt;Internal Audit Manager&lt;/strong&gt;, you will lead and carry out audits of Operations, Compliance and Technology across our crypto business, in line with the Internal Audit plan. You will work with Internal Audit leadership to identify risks, document and test controls, and recommend improvements, and you will help share risk information between the regulated entities, Robinhood Markets (RHM) leadership and the Board.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our Luxembourg office, with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and run audits of Operations, Compliance and Technology processes in our crypto business, from scoping through final reporting, in line with the Internal Audit plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform walkthroughs, control testing and substantive testing, and prepare work papers, flowcharts, narratives and risk and control matrices (RCMs) that document your procedures, findings and conclusions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clear audit findings that state the issue, its root cause and its business impact, and agree on recommendations with the teams you audit and with leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build RCMs for new audit areas, focusing on the controls that best reduce the highest risks, and assess whether policies, procedures and systems are adequate and efficient.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Business, Risk, Compliance, Legal and Technology partners to understand their processes, solve problems and recommend process improvements, while managing several audits and ad hoc requests at once.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of external or internal audit experience at a company that provides financial products or services, including evaluating internal controls or compliance programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience assessing the design and effectiveness of controls at a crypto exchange, market maker, custody provider, broker-dealer or similar financial institution, and working knowledge of crypto-asset regulations. Broker-dealer regulation knowledge is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting regulatory examinations, including preparing for them and responding to regulator questions and findings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor&#39;s degree in Audit, Finance, Operations or Technology, or equivalent practical experience. Certifications such as Certified Internal Auditor (CIA) or Certified Information Systems Auditor (CISA), or crypto and brokerage certifications, are a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in written and spoken English, strong analytical and problem-solving skills, and the ability to manage multiple projects on time in a fast-changing, regulated, international setting. Occasional travel is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenging, high-impact work to grow your career&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance driven compensation with multipliers for outsized impact, and bonus programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Top tier benefits to fuel your work, including supplemental health insurance, ancillary insurance, and mental health support programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to the best AI tools on the market and continuous AI skill-building for every employee, technical or not&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifestyle wallet - a highly flexible employer-paid benefits spending account expenses beyond traditional benefits such as wellness, childcare, learning, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge including company holidays, paid time off, sick time, paid volunteer time off, parental leave, and more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional office experience with catered meals, events, and comfortable workspaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly commuter stipend to help offset in-office commuting costs&lt;/li&gt;
