&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in program and/ or project management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong preference for a candidate that’s previously worked in a high velocity Events Marketing environment, and has previously worked in a highly regulated industry.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate excellent communication, organizational, and time-management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to organize information quickly and at a high level in order to address potential roadblocks, define the best way forward, and communicate trade-offs where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills - can analyze and interpret data to inform marketing decisions and identify risk in projects and programs early so that mitigation steps can be taken.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating and driving work independently in a dynamic environment, and comfortable navigating ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of asset creation (i.e. Creative, Production, etc.) and approval cycles (Stakeholder Reviews, Legal Approvals, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ideal candidate can build positive relationships with stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for democratizing finance and a deep understanding of Robinhood&#39;s mission, products, and target customers.&lt;/li&gt;
