&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world&#39;s biggest financial problems. We&#39;re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it&#39;s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We&#39;re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Robinhood Advisor Products team&lt;/strong&gt; is bringing Trade PMR, Robinhood&#39;s newly acquired registered investment advisor platform, into the Robinhood product suite. Our multiyear mission is to connect Robinhood&#39;s growing retail customers with Trade PMR&#39;s financial advisors, while bringing together two sets of technology and user experiences into one coherent product. You&#39;ll work alongside engineers, product managers, and partners in marketing and finance who care about getting this integration right for customers on both sides. We&#39;re energized by the scope of this work and the chance to shape how two strong businesses come together!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Staff Web Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;on this team, you&#39;ll build and scale full-stack systems, spanning backend services and web applications that support Advisors and Investors. You&#39;ll take on system design work, reasoning through tradeoffs to produce architecture that holds up as the integration between Trade PMR and Robinhood grows, and you&#39;ll stay hands-on, writing code while also setting technical direction. You&#39;ll partner with product, marketing, and finance stakeholders to turn open-ended requirements into concrete technical plans, and you&#39;ll coach and review other engineers&#39; work to raise the bar on quality and process across the team. You&#39;ll have an initial focus on integrating &quot;growing good&quot; retail customers with Trade PMR advisors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our New York, NY office(s), with in-person hybrid attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build full-stack web systems, backend services and user-facing web applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create system and technical designs that hold up at scale, and reason through tradeoffs with your team before committing to an approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with other engineering teams, product, marketing, and finance stakeholders to turn ambiguous requirements into clear technical plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and review other engineers&#39; work, helping raise the bar on code quality, design rigor, and delivery practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define mechanisms to ensure best practices are applied in our development cycle.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly with technical and non-technical audiences, including customers when needed, about progress and tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of professional engineering experience, with several years at the staff level and prior Team Lead experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building and scaling web systems, with strength in React, TypeScript, and Node, plus proficiency in Go and Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and reasoning about scalable, reliable architectures at the Staff Engineer (IC6) level or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An instinct for what users need and the judgment to turn that into sound product decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills for working with technical and non-technical stakeholders alike&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to have: experience building with AI-assisted workflows and shipping AI-powered features, and iOS or Android development experience.&lt;/li&gt;
